# Source-tree exclusions for Dockerfile `COPY . .`. Keeps the build context
# lean so per-image weight stays around code + node_modules dep graph instead
# of every previous worktree's checkout, every agent's transcript, every
# claude-code cache, and the entire content-addressable pnpm store. Without
# this list, the panel-managed overstory state (which lives in the workspace
# via bind mounts at runtime) inflates every image by 2-3 GB and tips the
# docker daemon into "input/output error" on layer extraction the moment two
# stacks share a disk.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs / dev caches
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo
coverage
**/coverage

# Repo-local pnpm content-addressable store. Containers get their own
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` during the `deps` stage; the host store is
# a host-only optimisation and including it in the image is just wasted bytes.
.pnpm-store
**/.pnpm-store

# Overstory + ecosystem state managed by the panel via bind mounts at
# runtime. Worktrees in particular hold full checkouts of completed agents
# and would otherwise be COPYed into every image rebuild.
.overstory
.canopy
.mulch
.seeds
.stack.json
.stack.start.log
.pgdata
.turbo-watch.pid
.turbo-watch.log

# Agent-side claude / playwright / test artefacts that have no place inside
# the app image.
.claude
.playwright

# VCS + secrets
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
*.log

# Docs (the boilerplate ships with hundreds of MB of generated docs)
*.md
!README.md
pgdata
